{"availability":"available","full":"jquatier/squinch","name":"squinch","description":"A skill for AI coding agents that draws clean, professional architecture diagrams as code: real cloud icons, zoomable from the landscape down to one service, exported as SVG, PNG or interactive HTML.","category":"Design","language":"TypeScript","stars":3,"forks":0,"created":"2026-07-25T01:24:14Z","updated":"2026-10-11T00:43:08Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"https://squinch.cc","topics":["agent-skills","ai","architecture","architecture-diagrams","aws","azure","c4","claude-code","codex","diagrams","diagrams-as-code","kubernetes","llm","svg","vscode-extension"],"demo":"https://squinch.cc/playground/","color":"#302e55","ink":"#dbd2ff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.088Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.088Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.088Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.088Z","stars":3,"forks":0}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["squinch (n.) — the corner arch that lets a round dome sit on a square room; the piece of architecture that makes mismatched structures fit together.","Your AI coding agent already knows the architecture — now it can draw it. Squinch is a skill for AI coding agents: describe the system in a paragraph and the agent writes a small, readable model that renders as a clean, professional diagram — real cloud icons, layout you steer without placing a box, and altitudes you can zoom through, from the whole landscape down to one service's internals.","Auto-layout tools give you no recourse when the picture comes out wrong: add a node and everything reshuffles, edges cross, and your only option is to accept it. Manual tools give you control but an un-diffable file. Squinch takes the third path — excellent auto-layout by default, plus relative hints (never pixel coordinates) that both humans and LLMs can reason about:"],"features":["LLMs write it fluently. Give your coding agent the bundled","skill and ask for a diagram of your system. The language was designed for agents to author rather than retrofitted for them, so what comes back is a correct diagram, not one you have to redraw.","1,358 real vendor icons. AWS, Azure, Google Cloud, Kubernetes and product logos, not","grey boxes with labels on them.","Auto-layout that gets it right, and lets you overrule it. Good diagrams"],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jquatier/squinch/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"b5a44127d1d0cf528b2987742d5a357faef5300f5e9cc317dd556ac9a80f87bc","extractedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.248Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.248Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"squinch (n.) — the corner arch that lets a round dome sit on a square room; the piece of architecture that makes mismatched structures fit together.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jquatier/squinch/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[{"text":"skill and ask for a diagram of your system. The language was designed for agents to author rather than retrofitted for them, so what comes back is a correct diagram, not one you have to redraw.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jquatier/squinch/blob/main/README.md"}],"requirements":[],"fingerprint":"b5a44127d1d0cf528b2987742d5a357faef5300f5e9cc317dd556ac9a80f87bc","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jquatier/squinch/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.249Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-10-11T00:43:08Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/jquatier/squinch/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-11T02:10:48.250Z","hash":"b5a44127d1d0cf528b2987742d5a357faef5300f5e9cc317dd556ac9a80f87bc","originalBytes":32447,"storedBytes":32447,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["squinch","one","packages","icons","agent","diagram","every","skill","view","diagrams","render","what","aws","google","each","icon","never","architecture","docs","file","pack","same","svg","system","two","when","edge","it.","nothing","